<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Andina starts.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Andina starts.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- ING Barings analyst Marla Marron has started coverage of Chilean bottler Embotelladora Andina with a rating of hold.</p>
<p>-- In a Feb 21 report, Marron said volumes in the Argentine market by an estimated five to six percent in 1997 and the company should garner economies of scale in Argentina from the addition of a new territory in mid-1996.</p>
<p>-- &quot;However, pricing in Brazil remains under substantial pressure and is unlikely to strengthen in 1997.&quot;</p>
<p>-- The company's American Depositary Receipts were up 1/4 to 36-1/8 in New York at midday.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
</text>
